  "whatChangedFrom001": [
    "Shape: every part is assembled from rock chunks (boulders, leaning slabs, hexagonal basalt columns, scree) fused by a voxel remesh and decimated; straight walls have top lines between about 2.8 and 5.9 m within one piece, overhanging slabs, broken columns and scree at the foot; any triangle larger than 1 m2 (walls/gate), 2.5 m2 (cave) or 6 m2 (backdrop) is split and bumped, so no large flat face remains (per-part maxFaceAreaM2 in kit.json).",
    "Seams: the ends of straight walls (x = +-2) are low boulder saddles that overlap the neighbour by up to 0.35 m; the middle is higher (\"ends lower, middle higher\").",
    "Texture: a cel-shaded bake instead of projected noise tiles - quantised key light from the part-local upper left using the Codex palette (#2b1e1f / #3a282a / #492c2c / #5b3837 / #6e413f / #a6624c), one flat colour per face with a soft gradient, rim highlight on convex edges, a few crisp 10 cm dark cracks (2 m cells), soft AO; no fine noise.",
    "Glow: orange cracks only below ~0.9 m and sparse (2.5%% of all covered texels; every wall part is under 5%%, kit.json lists emissiveFraction per object); the gate door carries a glowing seam and a carved ring/tick pattern (no text); the cave glows only deeper than z = -2 inside the tunnel.",
    "Previews: warm key light from the upper left, dark red-brown sky, no purple; player_view uses the 001 camera with the game ground tiled every 2.5 m and the Codex volcano_duck_0 / volcano_side_0 billboards in the corridor; compare_001_002.png renders the delivered 001 FBX in the same shot.",
    "Only walls, gates, cave and backdrop rocks were built (wall_straight x4, backdrop_rock x4, corners/end x3, gate x2, cave x1); obstacles, vents and the altar were dropped as requested."
  ],
  "deviations": [
    "control.py API v1 still only produces whole scenes; the official pipeline (capabilities -> plan -> validate -> generate -> inspect) was run unchanged into runs/spellduel-volcano-kit-002 for the run record and style reference, and the parts were built by the stand-alone kit_builder_v2.py in the job folder. No generator source file was modified.",
    "Texel density: the whole kit shares one 2048 atlas, so walls get about 31-35 texels per metre instead of the requested 128 (backdrops ~10-13, cave ~20). The cel style uses flat colour regions and 10 cm crack lines, which stay clean at 3 m; a 4096 atlas would be needed for 128 px/m.",
    "Hand-painted look is approximated procedurally: quantised lighting bands, per-face colour variation and rim highlight are computed in the bake shader rather than painted by hand; the facets of the low-poly mesh provide the \"one colour per rock face\" read.",
    "Backdrop rocks (budget 1500 triangles, 10-23 m tall) cannot keep every face under 1 m2; their largest faces are up to 6 m2 (listed per part). Cave faces are kept under 2.5 m2.",
    "Lighting is baked in part space (lit side toward the part's +X); instances rotated by 180 degrees show the shadow side toward the player. Use an Unlit material if the game adds its own real-time key light to avoid double shading.",
    "The 001 half of compare_001_002.png is rendered under the new warm lighting (not the 001 purple preview) so only the models and textures differ.",
    "Import was verified in a throwaway Unity 2022.3 project for the identical exporter settings in 001, not inside the SpellDuel project this time. Mobile frame rate was not measured."
  ],
